### Implement responsive chart resizing with window event listener in Lightweight Charts

Source: https://github.com/tradingview/lightweight-charts/blob/master/website/tutorials/customization/assets/step10.html

This snippet shows how to make a Lightweight Chart responsive to window resizing events. It attaches an event listener to the 'window' object that calls the chart's 'resize' method with the current window dimensions whenever the window size changes. This ensures the chart adapts to different screen sizes.

```javascript
// Adding a window resize event handler to resize the chart when
// the window size changes.
// Note: for more advanced examples (when the chart doesn't fill the entire window)
// you may need to use ResizeObserver -> https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/ResizeObserver
window.addEventListener("resize", () => {
    chart.resize(window.innerWidth, window.innerHeight);
});
```

